			"Message": "feat(Project): Fill IPC surface gaps and synchronize all 8 Element submodules\n\nAdvance Air, Cocoon, Common, Maintain, Mountain, Rest, Sky, and Wind to their latest commits, collectively closing multiple VS Code Workbench IPC compatibility gaps and enabling terminal window-reload persistence.\n\n**Mountain (largest delta — 479 insertions):**\n- Complete terminal state serialization/revival cycle (`SerializeTerminalState`, `ReviveTerminalProcesses`) so PTY sessions survive browser-style workbench reloads.\n- Wire six new language provider registrations (inline completion, inline edit, multi-document highlight, mapped edits, document paste, document drop) via `CreateProviderEffect` for VS Code >=1.87 API coverage.\n- Implement `configuration:inspect`, `configuration:lookup`, `themes:getColorTheme` IPC handlers and unwrap `ShowOpenDialog`/`ShowSaveDialog` envelope shapes for Wind consumer expectations.\n- Convert sandbox config path fields from `file://` URLs to OS-native paths to prevent double-encoding in `AbstractNativeEnvironmentService`.\n- Stub `log:registerLogger`/`log:createLogger` to prevent boot-time crashes and register terminal show/hide gRPC handlers.\n\n**Common:**\n- Add five IPC channel definitions via `DefineChannels!` — `ConfigurationInspect`, `ConfigurationLookup`, `ExtensionsGetManifest`, `ExtensionsResetPinnedState`, `ThemesGetColorTheme` — completing gaps in the protocol surface.\n\n**Cocoon:**\n- Rebuild all 40 Target/ ESBuild bundles against the refreshed RouteManifest, now tracking 130 Mountain RPC methods (up from 120) including the new language providers and terminal visibility toggles.\n\n**Wind:**\n- Regenerate upstream stubs to match the current VS Code source layout and add the five new IPC channels from Common to the Mountain-Wind boundary catalog.\n\n**Docs/naming consistency (Air, Maintain, Rest, Sky):**\n- Replace Unicode typographic dashes with ASCII hyphens in rustdoc HTML, Mermaid diagram labels, and inline comments to ensure consistent rendering across platforms and match codebase conventions.\n\nThese changes complete the terminal persistence cycle, extend VS Code API compatibility through VS Code 1.87, and synchronize all build artifacts and documentation with the expanded IPC surface.",
			"SHA": "ba4e373ce3aa8de27da936c240831380df32ea5d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T04:44:49Z",
